<!-- JOURNEY -->
<section style="padding-top:0">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head">
      <div class="eyebrow">Design journey</div>
      <h2>From pitch to production in seven weeks</h2>
      <p class="lede">I presented design progress at every weekly client review. Each step built on the last.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="journey2">
      <aside class="jdate" aria-hidden="true"><div class="jbig" id="jbig">May 11 – 17</div><div class="jstage" id="jstage">Concepts</div><ol class="jlist" id="jlist"><li class="on">May 11 – 17</li><li>May 18 – 27</li><li>May 28 – Jun 3</li><li>Jun 4 – 10</li><li>Jun 24</li></ol></aside>
      <div class="stops">

      <article class="stop" data-i="0">
        <div class="date">May 11 – 17<small>Concepts</small></div>
        <div class="body">
          <span class="pill-tag ghost">Brand concepts</span>
          <h3>Two directions, pitched before the contract</h3>
          <p><b>TILO</b>, a friendly helper, and <b>TILBY</b>, an expert advisor. Each came with a name, mark and previews in the chat and website so the client could judge it in context.</p>
          <p class="q">"A lively robot incorporating tile elements, captured both the personality of TILO and our brand identity."<small>DANNI WANG, CLIENT</small></p>
          <div class="media"><figure class="shot"><img src="/media/tilo/tl-concepts.jpg" alt="Concept 1 TILO, Hey ask Tilo, chosen; Concept 2 TILBY, knows every tile"></figure></div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="stop" data-i="1">
        <div class="date">May 18 – 27<small>Brand system</small></div>
        <div class="body">
          <span class="pill-tag ghost">Guidelines + chat entry</span>
          <h3>TILO chosen; it learns to say hello</h3>
          <p>With the agreement signed, I turned the mark into a brand system (above) and designed the first touchpoint: a light "Need Help?" tooltip that invites shoppers into chat without interrupting them.</p>
          <div class="media"><figure class="shot"><video src="/media/tilo/proto-tilo-chatbot.mp4" poster="/media/tilo/proto-tilo-chatbot-poster.jpg" autoplay muted loop playsinline aria-label="Prototype: the Need Help tooltip appears beside the TILO chat button"></video></figure></div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="stop" data-i="2">
        <div class="date">May 28 – Jun 3<small>Entry &amp; UX review</small></div>
        <div class="body">
          <span class="pill-tag ghost">Photo matching + UX review</span>
          <h3>The camera moves into the search bar; results start to sell</h3>
          <p>At the client's request I moved photo matching into the search bar with the new TILO camera icon. Then I tested the build as a shopper and redesigned the result card: larger square images, match badges, price first, View Product as the main action. Seven of my recommendations entered the official requirements list.</p>
          <div class="media two">
            <figure class="shot"><video src="/media/tilo/proto-camera.mp4" poster="/media/tilo/proto-camera-poster.jpg" autoplay muted loop playsinline aria-label="Prototype: the TILO camera button inside the search bar"></video></figure>
            <figure class="shot"><img src="/media/tilo/tl-cards.jpg" alt="Result card before and after the redesign"></figure>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="stop" data-i="3">
        <div class="date">Jun 4 – 10<small>Data</small></div>
        <div class="body">
          <span class="pill-tag ghost">Admin dashboard · beyond scope</span>
          <h3>A dashboard the store team can read</h3>
          <p>Not in the brief. I proposed and designed the admin panel: an overview landing page, chat history with confidence and ratings, two-level navigation, and month-over-month comparisons.</p>
          <div class="media"><figure class="shot"><img src="/media/tilo/dash-insights.jpg" alt="Before and after: metric tiles gained month-over-month change and comparisons with the daily average"></figure></div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="stop end" data-i="4">
        <div class="date">Jun 24<small>Live</small></div>
        <div class="body">
          <span class="pill-tag">Final delivery</span>
          <h3>TILO goes live on tileshoppes.com</h3>
          <p>Brand assets handed over: light and dark logo files, UI icons, tooltip assets and the 7-page guidelines. The TILO camera now sits in the site's search bar, and the TILO chat button greets every visitor.</p>
          <div class="closing">
            <div class="eyebrow">Closing the loop</div>
            <p>I didn't stop at the logo. The same thread runs from the first concept to the dashboard the client uses to judge TILO every day.</p>
            <div class="loop" aria-label="Idea, brand, experience, launch, data"><span>Idea</span><i>→</i><span>Brand</span><i>→</i><span>Experience</span><i>→</i><span>Launch</span><i>→</i><span class="on">Data</span></div>
            <figure class="dash"><img src="/media/tilo/dash-overview.jpg" alt="TILO Admin Panel overview: daily activity, monthly matches, cost, messages and sessions, peak days and snapshots"></figure>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- TESTIMONIAL -->
<section style="padding-top:0">
  <div class="wrap">
    <hr class="rule" style="margin-bottom:96px">
    <div class="testi">
      <div class="mark" aria-hidden="true">“</div>
      <div>
        <blockquote>She translated AI technology into a brand experience that felt natural and consistent with The Tile Shoppe. <em>We loved the result.</em> Beyond the visual design, Serena consistently made thoughtful recommendations that improved the overall product experience.</blockquote>
        <p class="who"><b>Danni Wang</b>, Operations Manager, The Tile Shoppe · LinkedIn recommendation, August 2026</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- REFLECTION -->
<section style="padding-top:0">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head"><div class="eyebrow">Reflection</div><h2>What I'd carry forward</h2></div>
    <div class="refl">
      <div><h3>A brand grows inside the product</h3><p>People remember TILO through the camera in the search bar, the tooltip that says hello and one orange language across the results.</p></div>
      <div><h3>Give choices, then reasons</h3><p>Two genuinely different directions, shown in real screens, let a non-design client decide quickly.</p></div>
      <div><h3>Big-company practice, small team</h3><p>Weekly reviews and a shared requirements tracker brought Tencent-scale product habits to a three-person team.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

